{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem, we need to identify the three-digit cubes that are the cubes of either squares or cubes. Let's break it down step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Identify the range of three-digit numbers\nThe smallest three-digit number is 100 and the largest is 999.\n\n### Step 2: Determine the range of \\( n \\) for which \\( n^3 \\) is a three-digit number\nWe need to find the smallest and largest integers \\( n \\) such that \\( 100 \\leq n^3 \\leq 999 \\).\n\n- For the smallest \\( n \\):\n  \\[\n  n^3 \\geq 100 \\implies n \\geq \\sqrt[3]{100} \\approx 4.64\n  \\]\n  Since \\( n \\) must be an integer, the smallest \\( n \\) is 5.\n\n- For the largest \\( n \\):\n  \\[\n  n^3 \\leq 999 \\implies n \\leq \\sqrt[3]{999} \\approx 9.997\n  \\]\n  Since \\( n \\) must be an integer, the largest \\( n \\) is 9.\n\nThus, \\( n \\) ranges from 5 to 9.\n\n### Step 3: List the three-digit cubes of integers from 5 to 9\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n5^3 &= 125, \\\\\n6^3 &= 216, \\\\\n7^3 &= 343, \\\\\n8^3 &= 512, \\\\\n9^3 &= 729.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\n","prefix_end":975,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1184,311,10542,279,2326,48342,54104,429,525,279,54104,315,2987,31340,476,54104,13,6771,594,1438,432,1495,3019,553,3019,382,14374,14822,220,16,25,64547,279,2088,315,2326,48342,5109,198,785,24632,2326,48342,1372,374,220,16,15,15,323,279,7772,374,220,24,24,24,382,14374,14822,220,17,25,29901,279,2088,315,17767,308,1124,8,369,892,17767,308,61,18,1124,8,374,264,2326,48342,1372,198,1654,1184,311,1477,279,24632,323,7772,25780,17767,308,1124,8,1741,429,17767,220,16,15,15,1124,273,80,308,61,18,1124,273,80,220,24,24,24,1124,3593,12,1752,279,24632,17767,308,1124,982,220,1124,9640,220,308,61,18,1124,709,80,220,16,15,15,1124,6383,550,308,1124,709,80,1124,26888,58,18,15370,16,15,15,92,1124,48053,220,19,13,21,19